    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_82f9459d",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: should_the_government_no_cat; hasOverallIntent: Propaganda; overall-intent-description: The image features a close-up of a cat with intense blue eyes, overlaid with the text 'should the government...' followed by a large 'no' at the bottom. The cat's expression is used as a visual metaphor to convey a strong, dismissive, or negative stance toward government intervention or policy. This is a common meme format used to express opposition to governmental actions or proposals in a humorous or sarcastic way. The overall intent is to influence opinion by leveraging the universally recognized 'angry cat' or 'disapproving cat' visual to signal 'no' to a political or social question. There is no toxicity present; the meme is satirical and does not target any specific group or individual based on protected characteristics. The intent is purely to convey a political or social opinion through visual and textual juxtaposition, functioning as a form of propaganda by association.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_9284fb61"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
